.TH DANBY-MODELING 1
.SH NAME
danby-modeling \- explore assumptions, parameters, and predictions in a differential-equation model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/modeling
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Danby-modeling
opens an interactive laboratory for the normal-form system
.IP
dx/dt = ax - y - (x squared + y squared)x,
.IP
dy/dt = x + ay - (x squared + y squared)y.
.PP
The green curve is the nonlinear model and the ochre curve is its linear
approximation at the equilibrium.  The phase portrait and time history show
that specifying equations is also specifying assumptions: the cubic term is
negligible near the origin but controls the global prediction.
.PP
Click the scale at the bottom to vary
.I a.
Space pauses and
.B r
resets the initial condition.
.SH SEE ALSO
danby-stability(1), numerics(2), plot(2)
